ren":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["05"]},"Avoid any “investment-based senior care” schemes that require upfront payments: card enrollment, prepaid care fees, buying senior housing units, travel-based care programs, and sales of senior products all fall under the same category of illegal fundraising"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/17-06"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["06"]},"Apart from the housing reverse mortgage insurance offered by insurers, you should avoid all other “housing-for-pension” schemes — never mortgage your home to buy financial products"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/17-07"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["07"]},"For elderly individuals at home who are bedridden or severely disabled, apply to the local yibao (basic medical insurance) office for long-term care insurance; it is not limited to seniors only"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/17-08"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["08"]},"For families with someone bedridden at home, pressure ulcers are a top concern: use an electric alternating-pressure air mattress, turn the patient regularly, and check bony areas daily"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/tip/17-09"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["09"]},"If an older person’s cataracts already affect walking safely, have an eye doctor assess surgery; when both eyes are affected, do not delay the second eye too long"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"aria-current":"page","className":"active","href":"/en/tip/17-10","data-status":"active"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["10"]},"When an older person walks a dog, hold the leash in the palm and never wrap it around the hand, keep the leash short, and train the dog first not to lunge forward on the leash"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-tip-page"},"children":[{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-breadcrumb","aria-label":"Breadcrumb"},"children":[{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book"},"children":["Explore the book"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"aria-hidden":"true"},"children":["/"]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"/en/book/17"},"children":["Chapter 17"," ·"," ","Having elderly family members at home"]}]},{"tag":"article","props":{"className":"life-entry-card status-unmarked is-standalone","id":"17-10"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-top"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-entry-number"},"children":["10"]},{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-evidence grade-b"},"children":["Evidence"," ","B"]}]},{"tag":"h1","props":{"lang":"en"},"children":["When an older person walks a dog, hold the leash in the palm and never wrap it around the hand, keep the leash short, and train the dog first not to lunge forward on the leash"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"lang":"en","className":"life-entry-summary"},"children":["In the US, fractures among people aged 65 and older while walking a leashed dog rose from about 1700 a year to about 4400, and eight in ten were women. The hip was the most common fracture site, and nearly three in ten needed hospital admission. About three-quarters of the hand injuries from dog leashes came from a leash wrapped around the hand and the dog pulling. So hold the leash in the palm, keep it short, and train the dog not to lunge."]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-impact"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["Holding the leash in the palm and shortening it costs noth…"]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["US emergency-department surveillance data, scaled up to national estimates, show fractures among people aged 6…"]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-actions","aria-label":"Mark: When an older person walks a dog, hold the leash in the palm and never wrap it around the hand, keep the leash short, and train the dog first not to lunge forward on the leash"},"children":[{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action done","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-check","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M20 6 9 17l-5-5"},"children":[]}]},"Done"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action todo","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-list-todo","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"rect","props":{"x":"3","y":"5","width":"6","height":"6","rx":"1"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m3 17 2 2 4-4"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 6h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 12h8"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M13 18h8"},"children":[]}]},"Plan to do"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-action favorite","aria-pressed":"false"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-bookmark","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m19 21-7-4-7 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h10a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v16z"},"children":[]}]},"Save"]}," ",{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"social-share-trigger"},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-share2 lucide-share-2","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"5","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"6","cy":"12","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"18","cy":"19","r":"3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"8.59","x2":"15.42","y1":"13.51","y2":"17.49"},"children":[]},{"tag":"line","props":{"x1":"15.41","x2":"8.59","y1":"6.51","y2":"10.49"},"children":[]}]},"Share this tip"]}]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button","className":"life-detail-toggle","aria-expanded":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"10","height":"10","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"currentColor","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-circle","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"circle","props":{"cx":"12","cy":"12","r":"10"},"children":[]}]},"Hide details"]},{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"16","height":"16","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-chevron-down rotated","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"m6 9 6 6 6-6"},"children":[]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-entry-details"},"children":[{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Cost"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["Holding the leash in the palm and shortening it costs nothing; walk with the older person once and show them. Training the dog not to lunge takes time. You can teach it yourself or hire a dog trainer, which costs money, and prices vary widely by region. The hard part is that older people are used to retractable leashes and to wrapping the leash around the wrist, so they have to change the habit."]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Benefit"]},{"tag":"p","props":{},"children":["US emergency-department surveillance data, scaled up to national estimates, show fractures among people aged 65 and older while walking a leashed dog rising from about 1671 in 2004 to about 4396 in 2017, a statistically significant increase. Of those with fractures, 78.6% were women and 28.7% were admitted to hospital. By single site, the hip was most common at 17.3%. By broad region, the upper limb was most common at 52.1%. In another set of national US emergency-department data (2001 to 2018), leash-related injuries were estimated at about 360000 visits (exact figure 356746). Of these, 193483 were from being pulled by the dog and 136767 were from tripping or getting tangled in the leash. Injuries per million people rose from 25.4 to 105.5. A hand-surgery clinic saw 443 patients with hand injuries from dog leashes over 5 years. About three-quarters were injured when a leash was wrapped around the hand or fingers and the dog pulled (the abstract gives 337 people, 75.9%). About one in five needed surgery (96 people, 21.6%). The US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention counted about 86629 fall injuries a year associated with cats and dogs in 2001 to 2006, of which 88.0% involved dogs. Among dog-related falls, 26% happened while walking the dog and 21.2% involved being pushed or pulled down by the dog"]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Original sources"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":["Pirruccio K, Yoon YM, Ahn J (2019). Fractures in Elderly Americans Associated With Walking Leashed Dogs. JAMA Surgery, 154(5), 458-459. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1001/jamasurg.2019.0061","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://doi.org/10.1001/jamasurg.2019.0061"]},"；Forrester MB (2020). Dog leash-related injuries treated at emergency departments. American Journal of Emergency Medicine, 38(9), 1782-1786. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ajem.2020.05.082","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ajem.2020.05.082"]},"；Plusch K, Givner D, Wiafe B, Lutsky K, Beredjiklian P (2026). Hand and Wrist Dog-Leash Injuries in the Outpatient Setting: A Review of 443 Cases. Hand, 21(4), 582-586. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1177/15589447241299128","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://doi.org/10.1177/15589447241299128"]},"；CDC (2009). Nonfatal fall-related injuries associated with dogs and cats — United States, 2001-2006. MMWR, 58(11), 277-281. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/mm5811a1.htm","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://www.cdc.gov/mmwr/preview/mmwrhtml/mm5811a1.htm"]},"；Rosa R, Buckley RE (2024). Leash-related injuries associated with dog walking: an understudied risk for dog owners? Journal of the American Veterinary Medical Association, 262(7), 973-978. ",{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.2460/javma.23.11.0608","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"children":["https://doi.org/10.2460/javma.23.11.0608"]}]},{"tag":"a","props":{"href":"https://doi.org/10.1001/jamasurg.2019.0061","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"life-source-link"},"children":["Open source link"," ",{"tag":"svg","props":{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"13","height":"13","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","strokeWidth":"2","strokeLinecap":"round","strokeLinejoin":"round","className":"lucide lucide-external-link","aria-hidden":"true"},"children":[{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M15 3h6v6"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M10 14 21 3"},"children":[]},{"tag":"path","props":{"d":"M18 13v6a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V8a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h6"},"children":[]}]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["Book note"]},{"tag":"p","props":{"className":"life-citations"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-content-reference"},"children":["Holding the leash in the palm instead of wrapping it around the hand is advice from the doctors at that hand-surgery clinic. They state that this protects the fingers and wrist but does not stop a lunging dog from pulling a person down. They also recommend a shorter leash: with a short leash the dog cannot build up speed, so the pull is lighter, while a long leash can also snag on things and trip the walker. A retractable leash extended to full length is a long leash. But no study has compared whether retractable or ordinary leashes cause more falls, and a 2024 review states there are no data on which type of leash was in use when injuries happened. Training the dog not to lunge on the leash was mentioned by the US CDC and by the authors of the fracture paper. That paper also suggests that older people who are thinking about getting a dog pick a smaller one. No study has calculated how many falls these measures prevent, so the benefit size is set as small by judgment. Whether bones can survive a fall: Section 1, item 39 (bone density screening) and item 40 (treat osteoporosis if found). Practicing balance in daily life: Section 1, item 13 (balance and leg strength). Whether dog walking counts as exercise: Section 2, item 44 (count dog walking toward walking volume). Main beneficiaries: your parents and grandparents."]}]}]},{"tag":"div","props":{"className":"life-personal-note"},"children":[{"tag":"span","props":{"className":"life-detail-label"},"children":["My note"]},{"tag":"button","props":{"type":"button"},"children":["Write a reminder for yourself…"]}]}]}]},{"tag":"nav","props":{"className":"life-tip-pager"},"chil